# Code Review Conventions

Apply these when writing or reviewing API code (from team CodeRabbit feedback).

## Layer boundaries

- Repository: data access only. Do not embed business/query policy (e.g. default category exclusions).
- Service: business rules, filter policy, cursor encoding/decoding validation, response mapping.
- Controller: HTTP only. Use `res.locals.validated` and auth helpers — never `(req as any).user`.

## Auth

- `requireAuth`: missing/invalid token → `401`.
- `optionalAuth`: missing or invalid token → treat as guest (`next()`), never `401`. Valid token → set `res.locals.user`.

## Validation (Zod)

- Define schemas in `src/schemas/*.schema.ts`.
- Apply via `validateRequest` on routes.
- Prefer `z.enum(PrismaEnum)` over deprecated `z.nativeEnum` (Zod 4).
- Controller must read validated input from `res.locals.validated` (query/params/body) — never cast raw `req.body`.
- `imageKeys`: non-empty strings, max count enforced in schema.
- `latitude` / `longitude`: validate geographic bounds when present.

## Repository

- Optional `DbClient` parameter for functions that may join a parent transaction.
- Soft delete: use `updateMany` with `deletedAt: null` for atomicity; check affected `count` in service.
- Permission checks: lightweight owner query (`id`, `userId` only) instead of full detail fetch.

## Cursor pagination

- Encode `{ id, sort, value }` (base64url JSON). Include `sort` so cursors cannot be reused across sort modes.
- Decode in service: reject sort mismatch, malformed values.
- Numeric cursor (`POPULAR`, `MOST_COMMENTED`): entire string must match `/^\d+$/` before parseInt.
- Date cursor (`LATEST`): value must be valid ISO and `new Date(value).toISOString() === value`.
- Repository: keyset condition + secondary `id` in `orderBy`. No AppError in repository.

## Images

- Use `toProfileImageUrl` from `profile-image.util.ts` — do not build S3 URLs inline.

## API responses

- List with pagination: `{ data: { items }, meta: { nextCursor, hasNextPage } }`.
- Detail: `{ data: { ... } }`.
- Errors: `AppError('ERROR_CODE')` with string keys.

## Git commits

- Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or other agent attribution to commits.
